            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AmberBread7946"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Try this using \"hot\" honey. The little bit of spice works wonderfully with the peanut butter. To further enhance it, make it on cinnamon raisin bread (I use wheat bread if I don't have cinnamon raisin in the house). To really step it up, slice a banana on top! Yum! I think I'll go make one now..",
            "datePublished": "2025-03-08T21:49:57.153Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cristy Webb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Drizzle a little honey on the bread and let it soak in before you spread the peanut butter mixture. It gives the bread a delightfully strange, honeycomby texture that adds an extra something to the sandwich.",
            "datePublished": "2020-06-10T19:15:22.900Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
